  "reading": {
   "title": "A problem at the bank",
   "text": "Last Tuesday Hafsa went to the bank because she saw a strange fee on her account. She took her card, her passport and a paper from the mail.\n\nAt the bank, a friendly clerk said hello. Hafsa explained, \"I have a problem. I didn't use my card last week, but there is a fee of twenty dollars.\" The clerk looked at his screen. \"I see the problem,\" he said. \"The bank made a mistake. You didn't do anything wrong.\"\n\nHe called the manager. The manager said sorry and removed the fee. Then the clerk asked Hafsa to sign a paper, and he gave her a receipt. Hafsa didn't understand every word, but she asked questions and the clerk answered slowly.\n\nShe left the bank happy. Later she told Linda, \"I didn't panic! I asked, and they solved the problem.\"",
   "glossary": [
    {
     "en": "clerk",
     "tr": "banka görevlisi"
